dn't change this stock installation setup.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4345865218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4345941827","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227#issuecomment-4345941827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227","id":4345941827,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABAwnPQw","user":{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T17:16:34Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T17:16:34Z","body":"> \"the user\" - root (not using systemd) - yes, can bind, if not headscale. No, cannot bind, if headscale. \n\nWhat happens if you run: `python3 -m http.server -b 0.0.0.0 80` as root?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4345941827/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4345973699","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227#issuecomment-4345973699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227","id":4345973699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABAwpLww","user":{"login":"esbeeb","id":33113557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTEzNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33113557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb","html_url":"https://github.com/esbeeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T17:21:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T17:23:37Z","body":"Works just fine:\n\n```\npython3 -m http.server -b 0.0.0.0 80\nServing HTTP on 0.0.0.0 port 80 (http://0.0.0.0/) ...\n```\nYes, it's like that twighlight zone episode where William Shatner is the only one who can see that frightening monster on the airplane wing","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4345973699/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4348046030","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227#issuecomment-4348046030","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227","id":4348046030,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABAynqzg","user":{"login":"esbeeb","id":33113557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTEzNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33113557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb","html_url":"https://github.com/esbeeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T22:40:44Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T23:02:22Z","body":"OK, I have more info about reproducing the bug, having talked in Discord:\nThe error messages are poor, that's the real problem here.\nHere's no problem binding to port 80, when config.yaml has these changes:\n\nserver_url: https://myrealdomain.com/\nlisten_addr: 0.0.0.0:80\ntls_letsencrypt_hostname: \"\"\n\nHere's where no possible binding to port 80 occurs:\n\nserver_url: https://myrealdomain.com/\nlisten_addr: 0.0.0.0:80\ntls_letsencrypt_hostname: \"myrealdomain.com\"\n\nNote the attempt to use letsencrypt on the 3rd line. That causes the error\n\nWhat will work (I have a working domain name in DNS):\n\nserver_url: https://myrealdomain.com/\nlisten_addr: 0.0.0.0:443\ntls_letsencrypt_hostname: \"myrealdomain.com\"\n\nNathanaël: \"When you set tls_letsencrypt_hostname, it will start an webserver on port 80 to serve the ACME validation file\nThat's why it doesn't work on your case, because you can't bind headscale + letsencrypt validation on same port (and let's encrypt require port 80)\"\n\nThe stock config.yaml could have been more helpful, by stating something like this, near \"listen_addr\":\n\n#If you don't plan to use headscale behind a reverse proxy - which would handle SSL itself - then you'll probably want SSL from LetsEncrypt, which headscale can obtain for you. So in that case use \"listen_addr: 0.0.0.0:443\" in production, in conjunction with stating your working DNS hostname that you'll use below, see \"tls_letsencrypt_hostname\"\n\nIn summary, the sensitivities of listen_addr and tls_letsencrypt_hostname (how they do or don't get along with each other) could be better explained in config.yaml\n\nAlso: The error message didn't mention the collision between headscale's use of port 80, and LetsEncrypt's use of port 80.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4348046030/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4352714307","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227#issuecomment-4352714307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3227","id":4352714307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABA3EmQw","user":{"login":"esbeeb","id":33113557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTEzNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33113557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb","html_url":"https://github.com/esbeeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esbeeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"